1
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,730
This is far enough.

2
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:15,680
Thank you, Shintaro.

3
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,390
Escher, get ready.

4
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:36,350
Right!

5
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,870
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,870
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

7
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:24,510
Episode 22: Black Dragon

8
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:24,750
That's enough! Don't do it again!

9
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:28,670
Don't use your power again, Mumbles!

10
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,630
You hear me?!

11
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:40,130
Stop!

12
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:40,770
Stop

13
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:43,010
You dumb son of a bitch!

14
00:02:45,650 --> 00:02:49,080
I got him! I saved the kid, Mumbles!

15
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:50,400
Come on!

16
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,950
Come on, man...

17
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:58,570
You gotta say something, Crow!

18
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:10,920
Dante! Could you help me?! 
There's more incoming!

19
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:15,670
<i>Is Bishop Dante not helping 
because he's an enemy?</i>

20
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:19,980
<i>He's scary looking... Maybe he 
really is working for him...?</i>

21
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:22,230
Ever so sorry.

22
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:27,680
I wish I could help more, but...

23
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:35,200
Bruise from poison punch

24
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:31,310
It seems your love is... heftier, 
than I expected, Ren.

25
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:34,500
That's not love! It's poison! 
What is this bishop's deal?!

26
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:40,710
Miss. Do you know who's 
responsible for this mess?

27
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:45,060
How about it?

28
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:49,720
<i>H-How... How do I answer this?</i>

29
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:52,490
<i>Whatever!</i>

30
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:52,220
Whatever!

31
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:54,400
I do.

32
00:03:55,550 --> 00:03:58,110
The one responsible for what's happening...

33
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:08,580
<i>Just like I thought.</i>

34
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:13,670
<i>His Luxa is a conjuration-type spell with 
the traits of purifying-type sorcery.</i>

35
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,110
<i>The issue is the specifics 
of that purification.</i>

36
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:22,970
<i>It has nothing to do with what 
the gods would define as evil.</i>

37
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:26,130
<i>He's the one making the 
distinction about what's evil.</i>

38
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:27,940
<i>And what is, consequently, purified.</i>

39
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:32,790
<i>Take a fireball, which ordinarily 
wouldn't be effected by purification...</i>

40
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:35,930
<i>Should Guitane decide as such,</i>

41
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,890
<i>it becomes evil, and is purified.</i>

42
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,730
<i>Those symbols are likely an indicator.</i>

43
00:04:43,730 --> 00:04:46,550
<i>I wonder what would happen if I came 
in contact with the one for me...?</i>

44
00:04:47,810 --> 00:04:49,280
<i>I'd like to know!</i>

45
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:52,380
<i>That said, the weaknesses are pretty clear.</i>

46
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:56,020
<i>One: it takes a few seconds 
to alter the symbols.</i>

47
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:01,080
<i>Two: he can't create a symbol that 
effects sorcery, in broad strokes.</i>

48
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:04,430
<i>If he could, he wouldn't need 
to alter it to affect flame,</i>

49
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:07,290
<i>barriers, and divine sorcery specifically.</i>

50
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:12,930
<i>Three: it looks like all of the divine sorcery 
symbols have been switched to flame.</i>

51
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:16,800
<i>So, does that mean he can only 
use three types at once?</i>

52
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:22,690
<i>That chimera body was fascinating 
enough, yet he goes as far as...</i>

53
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:26,820
<i>to tweak divine law—altering 
the mana signature of the gods.</i>

54
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,810
<i>He truly is...</i>

55
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:31,940
Abhowwent!

56
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:38,910
Kid. Can you make it to 
the shelter on your own?

57
00:05:38,910 --> 00:05:39,780
Yeah...

58
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:42,320
What about you?

59
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,450
I've got work to do.

60
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,070
Here's hoping you find your mom.

61
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:52,420
<i>As for me, I can't ditch a pal.</i>

62
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:56,970
What the hell do you think you're 
doing, you smoky lizard?

63
00:05:58,210 --> 00:06:01,530
I've had enough of your crap, asshole!

64
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:09,350
Everyone's in the clear, Crow!

65
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:12,070
You did it, man! Now we just gotta help you!

66
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,850
Get you back to the church 
for a purification...!

67
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:18,450
<i>Having a cheat power like 
making his words reality...</i>

68
00:06:18,450 --> 00:06:20,600
<i>obviously came with a hefty price!</i>

69
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:25,370
<i>Crow was coughing up blood 
every time he used his power!</i>

70
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:30,350
<i>Look how big this damn thing is... 
It's no wonder he pushing past his limits!</i>

71
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:34,910
<i>It must've been like trying to shove 
a watermelon up his nose, every time!</i>

72
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:38,620
<i>But he looked so damn happy!</i>

73
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:41,870
<i>Happy being able to use his 
powers to save people...!</i>

74
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:54,660
What...

75
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,840
are you...

76
00:06:59,170 --> 00:07:00,710
Laughing...?

77
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:03,960
You're dead, asshole.

78
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,940
<i>This damned lizard... was laughing...</i>

79
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:20,290
<i>this whole time... at us... at Crow...</i>

80
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:23,810
<i>At everything Crow's been through!</i>

81
00:07:24,990 --> 00:07:30,450
<i>Weird how just looking at him makes 
the crap he's been through clear.</i>

82
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:34,190
<i>What's weirder is, how we just met today....</i>

83
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:39,260
<i>And we barely even talked...</i>

84
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,190
<i>But I already feel like we're best bros!</i>

85
00:07:43,950 --> 00:07:45,380
Bring it on!

86
00:07:47,410 --> 00:07:49,210
Why would you do that?!

87
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:52,260
You're fighting me, got it?!

88
00:07:53,470 --> 00:07:54,840
Hey!

89
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:58,580
He's already dead, damn you!

90
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,350
Not yet!

91
00:08:07,350 --> 00:08:11,840
I can sense that Crow's still alive! 
The twin bishops are gonna patch him up!

92
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:13,840
<i>Crow's gang?</i>

93
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:16,900
Sorry to trouble you when 
you're exhausted, Tao, but...

94
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:19,600
I'm not tired! And I'm already doing it.

95
00:08:19,910 --> 00:08:23,050
It's okay. I can't sense any civilians.

96
00:08:23,050 --> 00:08:25,100
Crow's amazing!

97
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:28,690
He was able to protect 
them all from this beast!

98
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:30,710
He was an amazing warrior.

99
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:34,860
But it also means that this enemy was so 
strong that he could only hold it off...

100
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:38,080
Now, where do we begin?

101
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:41,230
How about I kick its butt, 
and you go for its face?

102
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:44,250
No. I'll go for the rear, 
you target the face.

103
00:08:44,250 --> 00:08:47,370
No way! That mug's too freaky! 
I get the butt!

104
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:02,160
Hyakkaken—

105
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,990
House of Langlis—

106
00:09:05,050 --> 00:09:07,020
Wheeling Twin Dragons!

107
00:09:16,030 --> 00:09:19,700
Unbelievable. This dragon... 
it was targeting...!

108
00:09:20,170 --> 00:09:22,720
My life flashed before my eyes! Again!

109
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,960
How many times is this gonna happen today?!

110
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:26,740
Tao! Your hand...

111
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,280
It's fine.

112
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:32,960
Stay focused! If we can't pull this 
off, everything goes to waste!

113
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,400
Everything Crow...

114
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:39,480
Everything we all did! 
This thing is enough to upend all of it!

115
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,600
<i>I've realized something.</i>

116
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,560
I'm sorry, Batts.

117
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:46,720
The boy... He's already...

118
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:52,170
<i>There's no stopping the infernal wyrm.</i>

119
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:00,000
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

120
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:00,000
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

121
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:06,200
<i>It was clear to me from 
the moment of my birth.</i>

122
00:10:08,030 --> 00:10:10,640
<i>The fact that I was a slave.</i>

123
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:18,220
<i>And that my lot in life would be to 
fly around with this man on my back.</i>

124
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:22,950
<i>I would act as loyal as a dog, 
as to not earn his displeasure,</i>

125
00:10:22,950 --> 00:10:25,730
<i>and I flew with all my heart and soul.</i>

126
00:10:26,470 --> 00:10:30,480
<i>And after a long, long trek 
over the great sea...</i>

127
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,230
Master Guisarme!

128
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:38,880
You've already grasped 
how to teleport things!

129
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:43,230
<i>My Master obtained the 
greatest power in the world.</i>

130
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:48,400
<i>I was as proud as I was terrified. 
He was my Master.</i>

131
00:10:48,950 --> 00:10:52,180
<i>And no one could stop him anymore...</i>

132
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:57,560
I think I'm done with this dragon, now.

133
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:16,770
I suppose detours can prove quite 
fruitful, every once in a while.

134
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:21,780
I wonder how long Lordost Island 
has been a den for devils?

135
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:24,030
He's a true monster.

136
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,280
The one inhabiting that manor...

137
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:33,450
Most likely the demon realm's nobility, 
the so-called Demon Lords.

138
00:11:33,450 --> 00:11:36,240
<i>Who is that human?</i>

139
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:40,170
<i>This is Lord Guisarme's territory.</i>

140
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:46,340
What do you suppose would happen if I 
cast my Luma Maxima on a demon lord?

141
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:48,780
The light of purification has a 
pronounced effect on his kind...

142
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:51,180
It would likely do substantial damage.

143
00:11:51,570 --> 00:11:53,430
<i>Aren't they afraid?</i>

144
00:11:54,220 --> 00:12:00,520
But what about his heart? 
Do you suppose it would become "clean"?

145
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:07,470
The answer is no. 
There is no purifying his heart.

146
00:12:07,470 --> 00:12:10,710
Which is to say, there is no taint to it.

147
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:14,960
The hearts of monsters are pristine.

148
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:20,970
They mean no harm. 
When they kill, or when they destroy,

149
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:23,930
or even when they abandon their comrades...

150
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:28,160
<i>And I somehow realized...</i>

151
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:31,960
<i>That this would be my next master.</i>

152
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:45,990
Please, put this chimera body 
to use however you see fit.

153
00:12:45,990 --> 00:12:49,200
<i>Guitane... that was why I followed him.</i>

154
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:53,000
It's my wish that you would use 
it to seek out your true nature.

155
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,760
<i>Over half of my body had been 
replaced with different parts,</i>

156
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:02,170
<i>without a single change 
to my dog-like mentality.</i>

157
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:05,560
<i>He could speak of my true nature, or freedom,</i>

158
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:08,310
<i>there was no way I could 
understand any of that.</i>

159
00:13:08,310 --> 00:13:11,550
If you have nowhere to go, 
you can come with me.

160
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:14,510
I'm preparing a rather grand event.

161
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:19,290
Although, I don't have much 
planned beyond that.

162
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:22,780
I'm lost myself, you see.

163
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,150
<i>I hope he finds his way.</i>

164
00:13:26,830 --> 00:13:28,180
<i>As for me...</i>

165
00:13:29,170 --> 00:13:31,410
<i>I think I'm beginning to understand...</i>

166
00:13:32,610 --> 00:13:34,670
<i>who it is I am!</i>

167
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:39,390
<i>He's had giant arms grafted onto him!</i>

168
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:43,540
<i>This dragon is a chimera too! 
We can't assume anything about it!</i>

169
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,460
Tao?!

170
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,940
<i>She took the full impact...</i>

171
00:13:49,510 --> 00:13:51,310
House of Langlis—

172
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:55,600
Double Tiger, Claw and Fang

173
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:08,240
<i>Oh, this is so much fun.</i>

174
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,610
<i>They're so adorable.</i>

175
00:14:10,610 --> 00:14:13,240
Sylpha! Damn it!

176
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:17,340
Come on! I'm begging you! 
You gotta heal him somehow!

177
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,740
<i>All of you...</i>

178
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,580
<i>Those faces you make...</i>

179
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:23,010
Batts! Let me treat your wounds!

180
00:14:23,010 --> 00:14:25,030
You're hurt badly too!

181
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:28,560
Who cares about me?! This guy's a hero!

182
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,730
<i>Your screams are what made it clear to me.</i>

183
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:37,770
Where's it... aiming...?

184
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:42,400
The shelter?!

185
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,730
Screw you!

186
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,410
<i>That I am strong...</i>

187
00:14:46,410 --> 00:14:49,410
<i>And I am cruel...</i>

188
00:14:51,370 --> 00:14:52,780
<i>Now...</i>

189
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:56,290
Damn it... move, body!

190
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:57,790
<i>More...</i>

191
00:14:58,110 --> 00:15:01,160
<i>Let me feel it more!</i>

192
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:04,290
I don't care... who does it...

193
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:07,700
God... or devil...!

194
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:11,050
<i>As I bathe in your hatred...</i>

195
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:13,930
<i>I feel the ecstasy of domination!</i>

196
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:22,700
Please, someone stop this forsaken dragon!

197
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,950
You did well to endure, good bishops.

198
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:52,850
We will take over from here.

199
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:56,970
I am going to focus on healing 
this one. Will that suffice?

200
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:58,180
Works for me.

201
00:15:58,570 --> 00:16:02,060
Make sure you save him. 
Crow's part of the crew.

202
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,530
So, Black Dragon...

203
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:12,240
Where the hell do you get off?

204
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:15,700
Who?

205
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:18,080
Er... I'm, uh...

206
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:22,800
Right! The wandering adventurer! Grimtaro!

207
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,930
Grim...taro?

208
00:16:24,930 --> 00:16:27,980
<i>I gotta admit, he's got 
quite the hottie aura.</i>

209
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:29,450
What are those horns?

210
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:35,910
Grim, huh?

211
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:35,910
Friend or foe?

212
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:35,910
Nice guy!

213
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:35,910
Maybe it's not him?

214
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:33,150
These are just... accessories! For my hair!

215
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,890
<i>This is so embarrassing!</i>

216
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:39,440
Do you realize that if you 
show up looking like that,

217
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:42,050
you're going to be mistaken 
for a monster or a chimera?

218
00:16:42,050 --> 00:16:43,650
Y-You got a point...

219
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:48,940
<i>I changed forms like Jihriel said, 
but it's so awkward trying to look human!</i>

220
00:16:50,590 --> 00:16:52,020
Regardless...

221
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:58,060
We're on your side. Crow's gonna be fine.

222
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:01,050
That blond guy, Jerkiel, is gonna save him.

223
00:17:01,050 --> 00:17:05,180
Who are you calling Jerkiel? 
But I will heal him.

224
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:10,680
Even a single fatality in this battle 
would justify me to taking my own life.

225
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:12,170
Tao.

226
00:17:13,150 --> 00:17:14,350
How do you know my—

227
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:16,550
There aren't any civvies around 
here anymore, right?

228
00:17:17,430 --> 00:17:18,790
All clear!

229
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:27,060
Then... let's raise some hell.

230
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:33,380
Hey.

231
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:39,620
You're not a pillbug. Quit rolling around.

232
00:17:42,730 --> 00:17:46,560
I heard you laughing, y'know.

233
00:17:47,090 --> 00:17:51,710
There's no way a black dragon from the 
Netherworld came to the human realm on its own.

234
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:54,720
Bet you were a lap dragon 
that got abandoned, huh?

235
00:17:55,910 --> 00:17:57,660
Pitiful little bastard.

236
00:17:58,090 --> 00:18:01,840
Hope you weren't counting on 
me taking pity on you, though.

237
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:05,490
Survival of the fittest... 
That's how it works in the Netherworld.

238
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:08,870
And you were trying play 
by those rules up here...

239
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:11,610
making a mess of my turf.

240
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:17,610
No pride, no nothing... just a rowdy mutt 
going nuts after getting off its chain.

241
00:18:17,990 --> 00:18:22,410
And you have the nerve to laugh? 
I can't even bring myself to kill you.

242
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:28,260
Tuck your tail between your legs and go home.

243
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:35,070
Th-That thing can fly?!

244
00:18:44,010 --> 00:18:46,190
<i>This demon...</i>

245
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,950
<i>is too kind!</i>

246
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:57,470
<i>After everything that's happened
to a wretch like me... he's still...</i>

247
00:18:58,150 --> 00:19:01,240
<i>trying to show me how to live like a dragon.</i>

248
00:19:02,130 --> 00:19:03,420
<i>Even now...</i>

249
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:06,960
<i>he grants me time I could use to escape.</i>

250
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:11,380
<i>Thank you... but I can't do that.</i>

251
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:15,940
<i>I can't turn my back on this 
swell of emotions I feel.</i>

252
00:19:17,170 --> 00:19:19,440
<i>I will live as a dragon...</i>

253
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:23,470
<i>and maybe die as one!</i>

254
00:19:24,050 --> 00:19:28,030
<i>Not filled with joy or fear... but pride!</i>

255
00:19:28,390 --> 00:19:33,230
Waah

256
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:33,230
<i>Having lived these many years... 
with a draconic roar!</i>

257
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:38,110
Dual incantation...

258
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:41,860
Arctis Obscura Forta Magnificat!

259
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:56,890
<i>We all had our own baggage.</i>

260
00:19:56,890 --> 00:20:01,900
<i>Were we all able to overcome our 
regrets during this battle?</i>

261
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:05,280
Lastly, please swallow this 
sphere with Luma Maxima.

262
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:11,390
By activating it, your rotting bodies will 
turn to dust, and your souls will be purified.

263
00:20:11,670 --> 00:20:14,020
When would you want to use it?

264
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:18,060
A good question. If you're being 
tortured in a way that's unbearable,

265
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:24,150
or if you have overcome your lingering 
feelings for the world, and yearn to pass on.

266
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:27,200
Would that be betraying me?

267
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:30,410
Of course not.

268
00:20:30,410 --> 00:20:36,930
I am simply using you all. 
I don't consider you comrades.

269
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,690
<i>I'm not so sure about that.</i>

270
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:44,560
<i>If nothing else, by meeting you, I was able 
to die in a way fitting for a dragon.</i>

271
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,830
<i>So, I won't use your sphere.</i>

272
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:50,940
<i>Guitane... I'll be seeing you in Hell.</i>

273
00:20:59,110 --> 00:20:59,650
Gulp

274
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:01,530
Blop

275
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:07,560
<i>I've been able to absorb a decent amount 
of mana since the seal was broken.</i>

276
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,960
<i>I'm stronger!</i>

277
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:12,580
<i>Maybe I could take a demon lord now...!</i>

278
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:13,960
Huh?

279
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:17,210
Nah, no way. Not yet, anyhow.

280
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:19,960
Which means...

281
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:24,760
I'm still nowhere close to that 
brat up above the clouds, yet.

282
00:21:26,070 --> 00:21:28,980
Come on. We'll get a glimpse 
of the apex, together.

283
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,490
Sorry for the delay.

284
00:21:32,490 --> 00:21:34,470
It's fine. How's Crow?

285
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:37,630
What kind of blast was that?!

286
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:37,630
He'll be fine. The worst part is over.

287
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:40,610
Hey! Where did that blond 
Jerkiel fellow go?!

288
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:42,760
But I'm exhausted. 
And can barely move anymore.

289
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,460
Look at how much better Crow looks!

290
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:47,870
The folks down there should 
be fine at this point.

291
00:21:47,870 --> 00:21:53,250
Right. And all we can do at this 
point is offer unsolicited advice...

292
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:55,940
Let's get going. Up above the clouds...

293
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:00,630
To the final battle!

294
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:38,760
<i>The name's Grimtaro! I'm an adventurer 
who was just passing through.</i>

295
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:40,630
<i>All the notable bad guys are down!</i>

296
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:43,340
<i>That just leaves the last 
battle, way up on high.</i>

297
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:45,240
<i>Next time, on episode 23:</i>

298
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,760
<i>"The Battle Above the Clouds."</i>

299
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:50,540
Episode 23

300
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:50,540
The Battle Above the Clouds

301
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:50,110
<i>You will witness the depths of sorcery.</i>

